/// Render a Handlebars template with the given data context.
/// Use #partials to register named partial templates (as a struct or map).
/// Use #strict to error on missing variables instead of rendering empty strings.
/// The data is written as JSON is, except that an abstract value is its
/// data alone and a map whose keys are scalars that print apart is an
/// object keyed by their text (`{{m.[1]}}` over `{1 => "one"}` is "one");
/// any other map is an array of `[key, value]` pairs.
val render: fn<'a: Data, 'b: Data>(?#strict: bool, ?#partials: 'a, template: string, data: 'b) -> Result<string, `HbsErr(string)>;
